      "locales": {
        "zh": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/0/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/0",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/0/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "1. 简述光的折射定律。",
          "prompt_sha256": "32ea5d1e5bff12370bc97184ebddaad78cd4128aa1eed2aa997c459477be214d",
          "displayAnswer": "在固定频率、均匀各向同性透明介质的几何光学模型中，入射光线、折射光线和入射点处的法线在同一平面内。\n两条光线位于法线两侧，入射角与折射角都从法线量起，满足 $n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2$。\n这里两种折射率对应同一频率；这不是反射角等于入射角的定律。",
          "display_answer_sha256": "5814b45f7d9ee47b5917aea70949c053dff87ba0476317e6a88fbe2fbc76449e",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        },
        "en": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/0/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/0",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/0/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "1. State the laws of refraction of light.",
          "prompt_sha256": "e7db185904e04fa7625a448cd92f73cc791ba4232f8ed4291ee064e0e3574a33",
          "displayAnswer": "For a fixed frequency in the geometrical-optics model of homogeneous, isotropic transparent media, the incident ray, refracted ray, and normal at the point of incidence lie in one plane.\nThe incident and refracted rays lie on opposite sides of the normal. With both angles measured from the normal, $n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2$.\nThe two refractive indices refer to the same frequency; this is not the law equating reflection and incidence angles.",
          "display_answer_sha256": "1e80cb645e683ed70080a275940aa60cc55224b95af4889f228c0be71f62e15d",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "N77-Q2",
      "original_pointer": "/exercises/1",
      "original_question": "2. 光的绝对折射率与相对折射率有什么区别？",
      "question_text_sha256": "6f9b0da4672d085b1a3dc660d120da62001c6e3a57d64c7d1df398a51ef32bdc",
      "source_number": "2",
      "group_id": "g1",
      "pages": [
        "p0206#5"
      ],
      "original_figure_refs": [],
      "raw_pointer": "/solutions/1",
      "raw_status": "INDEPENDENT_RAW_CONDITIONAL_NOT_APPROVED",
      "locales": {
        "zh": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/1/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/1",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/1/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "2. 光的绝对折射率与相对折射率有什么区别？",
          "prompt_sha256": "6f9b0da4672d085b1a3dc660d120da62001c6e3a57d64c7d1df398a51ef32bdc",
          "displayAnswer": "绝对折射率把真空中的光速与介质中的相速度比较：$n=c/v$。\n光从介质 1 进入介质 2 时，介质 2 对介质 1 的相对折射率为 $n_{21}=n_2/n_1=v_1/v_2$。\n它比较两种介质，而不是每种介质与真空；交换两种介质的顺序会把相对折射率变为倒数，所有速度与折射率都取同一频率。",
          "display_answer_sha256": "00876a499e7ec7283a8995da95d5d97eb85c9bae8089f83737175aca7fbc07d0",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        },
        "en": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/1/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/1",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/1/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "2. How does absolute refractive index differ from relative refractive index?",
          "prompt_sha256": "0d0f7aa62339c4f19adc773a94a56070d4ab964a319b56b9163290433541505e",
          "displayAnswer": "Absolute refractive index compares the vacuum speed of light with the phase speed in a medium: $n=c/v$.\nFor light going from medium 1 into medium 2, the index of medium 2 relative to medium 1 is $n_{21}=n_2/n_1=v_1/v_2$.\nThis compares two media rather than each medium with vacuum. Reversing their order gives the reciprocal relative index; all speeds and indices are evaluated at the same frequency.",
          "display_answer_sha256": "8ce17de6b2c6d138c2de24f3497e7460e54a4424e2e95ff41eb3538132740cbd",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        }
      }
    },
