          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/2/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/2",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/2/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "3. What determines the critical angle for total internal reflection?",
          "prompt_sha256": "877cffe6b0a420dc898c5228faa93464fb281cc20e5ee54d817ed6dd0f26d4cb",
          "displayAnswer": "At an ideal interface between transparent media, a critical angle for total internal reflection exists only for incidence from the higher-index medium into the lower-index medium, with $n_1>n_2$.\nMeasured from the normal, it is the incidence angle at which the refraction angle reaches a right angle, so $\\sin\\theta_c=n_2/n_1$.\nThus $\\theta_c=\\arcsin(n_2/n_1)$.\nTotal internal reflection occurs above the critical angle; equality is the limiting case of a refracted ray along the interface.",
          "display_answer_sha256": "c36e11dd8df66017019fe06cf5082fdabb430ce7bd4303f8987a00d667f40778",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        }
      }
