          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/3/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "4. 什么样的透镜叫薄透镜？",
          "prompt_sha256": "14e16bc65594c52ac16693049eb3b291db42705aef24e72617b4db3eff9cef21",
          "displayAnswer": "薄透镜是厚度相对于两面的曲率半径足够小、在所需精度下可以忽略厚度的透镜。\n在相应的近轴成像模型中，可以把两次折射近似归到一个透镜平面，不必分别追踪透镜内部的光路。\n“薄”描述厚度可以忽略，并不是说焦距必须很小或透镜一定会聚。",
          "display_answer_sha256": "c91e044aeaffd4ea83bcc2a302550e05509c01b60530548e1bcc87e04ac1e13b",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        },
        "en": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/3/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/3",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/3/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "4. What is a thin lens?",
          "prompt_sha256": "47549c088fa42480fc373741a9a977faa5eee609173ca641a9135d0d4f220886",
          "displayAnswer": "A thin lens has a thickness sufficiently small compared with the radii of curvature of its two surfaces that thickness can be neglected at the required accuracy.\nIn the corresponding paraxial imaging model, its two refractions can be represented at a single lens plane without separately tracking the path inside the lens.\nThinness means negligible thickness, not necessarily a short focal length or a converging lens.",
          "display_answer_sha256": "4a0d48fbb28459204c62ab3a0e6525cebf0fec8da988fbb76151cfb3a12657aa",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        }
      }
    },
