    {
      "id": "N77-Q6",
      "original_pointer": "/exercises/5",
      "original_question": "6. 写出透镜公式.",
      "question_text_sha256": "36ab14504b1ec1e7a618abca79d36afa6ad8b412f5b6aafd277f682715e62d87",
      "source_number": "6",
      "group_id": "g1",
      "pages": [
        "p0206#9"
      ],
      "original_figure_refs": [],
      "raw_pointer": "/solutions/5",
      "raw_status": "INDEPENDENT_RAW_CONDITIONAL_NOT_APPROVED",
      "locales": {
        "zh": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/5/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/5",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/zh/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/5/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "6. 写出透镜公式。",
          "prompt_sha256": "33beb201172892eb86bd9915cfa2758e813d5fa30f2755be836a7707e7a1323c",
          "displayAnswer": "对两侧为同一种介质的薄透镜，在近轴近似下：\n$\\frac{1}{d}+\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{F}$。\n其中物距为 $d$，像距为 $f$，焦距为 $F$，不可混淆像距与焦距。\n按本课约定，实物距、实像距和会聚透镜焦距取正；虚物距、虚像距和发散透镜焦距取负。\n虚物点指入射会聚光束在未经透镜改变时沿原方向会聚的位置；求解未知距离时保留它的带符号值。",
          "display_answer_sha256": "4b52830da47852eea1d6b1c7c61afb436b11ae8c1efb1ca371ba326e6295aec9",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        },
        "en": {
          "prompt_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/exercises.template.json",
          "prompt_pointer": "/exercises/5/text",
          "source_snapshot_pointer": "/source/data/exercises/5",
          "answer_file": "/Users/yong/.codex/worktrees/00b1/lemmadeck/.intentfold/tickets/STEMROBIN-181/tmp/d610-n77-first-written-answer-author/en/answer-keys.candidate.json",
          "answer_pointer": "/answers/5/displayAnswer",
          "prompt": "6. Write the lens formula.",
          "prompt_sha256": "ea9faba5afa205465737645ee239426ec38c40f029311981199b4010428d95ad",
          "displayAnswer": "For a thin lens with the same medium on both sides, in the paraxial approximation:\n$\\frac{1}{d}+\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{F}$.\nHere the object distance is $d$, image distance is $f$, and focal length is $F$; image distance and focal length are distinct.\nIn this lesson, real object distances, real image distances, and converging-lens focal lengths are positive; virtual object distances, virtual image distances, and diverging-lens focal lengths are negative.\nA virtual object is the point where incoming converging rays would meet without the lens changing them. Retain the signed value when solving for an unknown distance.",
          "display_answer_sha256": "de9e9dd4849157cf2ee3abe57d307a1a27a364a102c80d2e6c1718d7745f4748",
          "source": "derived",
          "grading": "ungraded",
          "parts": []
        }
      }
    },
